Takes draft 68's rule out of both hosts (DESIGN.md §7.3): an event for a
path a rule ignores is no longer an observation of the directory holding
it, in the daemon's watcher (`watched.rs`) or the simulator's
(`watch_ignored`). A received deletion held because its directory holds
ignored files then waits for the next full scan, up to an hour, after the
user removes the last of them. No seed fails with this patch, since the
final phase's scans observe every directory, so the rule's tests in both
hosts stand in.

test: delocal-sim sim::tests::removing_the_last_ignored_file_releases_a_held_deletion_without_a_scan
